      "summaries": {
        "en": "Dolt is a version-controlled SQL database that brings Git-like branching and merging to data, solving the challenge of tracking and collaborating on evolving datasets. Its technical innovation lies in implementing a content-addressable storage system with commit graphs and diffs for structured data, enabling granular version history. Developers can use Dolt as a drop-in MySQL replacement to create data branches, experiment with schema changes, and merge results, making it ideal for data science workflows, A/B testing datasets, and maintaining auditable data pipelines.",
        "zh": "Dolt 是一个版本控制的 SQL 数据库，将 Git 的分支与合并功能引入数据管理，解决了数据集演进过程中的追踪与协作难题。其核心技术在于为结构化数据实现内容寻址存储系统，通过提交图和差异记录实现细粒度的版本历史。开发者可以将其作为 MySQL 的替代品直接使用，创建数据分支进行实验性修改，并安全合并结果，适用于数据科学工作流、机器学习数据集版本管理以及需要完整审计轨迹的数据管道维护。",
        "es": "Dolt is a version-controlled SQL database that brings Git-like branching and merging to data, solving the challenge of tracking and collaborating on evolving datasets. Its technical innovation lies in implementing a content-addressable storage system with commit graphs and diffs for structured data, enabling granular version history. Developers can use Dolt as a drop-in MySQL replacement to create data branches, experiment with schema changes, and merge results, making it ideal for data science workflows, A/B testing datasets, and maintaining auditable data pipelines.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "dolt stands out for agent-memory, agent-memory-server, and ai-agents in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Dolt is a version-controlled SQL database that brings Git-like branching and merging to data, solving the challenge of tracking and collaborating on evolving datasets. Its technical innovation lies in implementing a content-addressable storage system with commit graphs and diffs for structured data, enabling granular version history. Developers can use Dolt as a drop-in MySQL replacement to create data branches, experiment with schema changes, and merge results, making it ideal for data science workflows, A/B testing datasets, and maintaining auditable data pipelines.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/dolthub/dolt for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
